---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Diagram from '../components/Diagram.astro';
import StageRail from '../components/StageRail.astro';
import { principles } from '../data/principles';
import { products } from '../data/products';
import { u } from '../lib/url';
---
<Base title="Hangar" description="Platform engineering from James Fillman's point of view, with Hangar, an internal developer platform built in the open, as the working implementation." section="home">
  <div class="wrap">
    <section class="hero">
      <p class="eyebrow">Platform engineering · James Fillman</p>
      <h1>Platforms are products, APIs and opinions. <em>Hangar</em> is mine, running.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This is where I write about platform engineering: how I think software should get from a developer's
        head to production, and what a platform owes the people who use it. Everything here is backed by
        Hangar, an internal developer platform I build in the open. It serves container apps and AI agent
        workloads through the same control plane, and it keeps changing as I learn.
      </p>
    </section>

    <Diagram id="plan/01-hangar-family" />

    <h2>Five things I build around</h2>
    <p class="lede">The same five ideas show up in every part of Hangar. Each page on this site comes back to them.</p>
    <div class="grid principles">
      {principles.map((p) => (
        <a class="card" href={u(`principles/#${p.slug}`)}>
          <span class="eyebrow">{p.n}</span>
          <h3>{p.name}</h3>
          <p>{p.claim}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>

    <h2>The whole SDLC, from the platform side</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      Seven stages, from design to improvement. Each one pairs an opinion with the part of Hangar that implements
      it, and says what changes when the author of a change is an AI agent rather than a person.
    </p>
    <StageRail />

    <h2>Six products, one Hangar</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      {products.map((p) => (
        <a class="card" href={p.repo}>
          <span class="eyebrow"><img class="mark" src={u(`marks/${p.key}-tile.svg`)} alt="" width="28" height="28" />{p.name}</span>
          <h3>{p.tag}</h3>
          <p>{p.role}</p>
        </a>
      ))}
    </div>

    <h2>Start here</h2>
    <div class="grid">
      <a class="card" href={u('cicd/')}><span class="eyebrow">CI/CD</span><h3>Seventeen practices, one worked example</h3><p>What I believe about CI/CD, told through Glidepath's architecture decision records.</p></a>
      <a class="card" href={u('autopilot/')}><span class="eyebrow">AI workloads</span><h3>Agents on a platform, bounded and audited</h3><p>Autopilot, in nineteen diagrams: how Hangar runs any AI agent workload.</p></a>
      <a class="card" href={u('platform/')}><span class="eyebrow">Architecture</span><h3>How the platform fits together</h3><p>The control plane, the delivery path and the pane of glass, for containers and agents.</p></a>
      <a class="card" href={u('log/')}><span class="eyebrow">Log</span><h3>What changed, and why</h3><p>Hangar is never finished. This is its history, one dated entry at a time.</p></a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
<style>
  .principles .card h3 { font-size: 1.25rem; }
</style>
